{# Shown (by the server, or live by help-form.js) when a help request is over
   HELP_MAX_CHARS. The id is what the script toggles. #}
<div id="too-long" class="too-long"{% if not tooLong %} hidden{% endif %}>
  <p>
    That request is over the {{ HELP_MAX_CHARS }}-character limit, so it won’t
    be submitted.
  </p>
  <p>
    It’s fine to be curious about where a system’s limits are. But actually
    abusing a system is antisocial: it just makes things work less well for
    everyone else. Please trim your request down to what you actually need help
    with.
  </p>
</div>
